# Build context hygiene.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here would otherwise be
# baked into an image layer. Two of these matter beyond image size: a host
# .env would put real credentials into a distributable layer, and a host
# vendor/ built on macOS would shadow the one composer installs in the image.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

vendor/
node_modules/

storage/logs/*.log
storage/framework/cache/data/*
storage/framework/sessions/*
storage/framework/views/*
database/*.sqlite

.git/
.gitignore
.phpunit.result.cache
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
